---
// Two-column intro under the hero. Client's own copy, supplied 28 Sept 2026,
// replacing the lorem ipsum this slot carried from the Elementor prototype.
//
// Both columns are paragraphs now. The left was an <h2>, which suited the
// short placeholder but not a 173-character sentence - a heading that long is
// wrong for screen readers and search alike. The page still has its headings
// further down ("Our Services", "Industries & Applications", and so on).
---

<section class="section">
  <div class="container grid">
    <p class="lead">
      As a drone survey specialist, Pixel Surveys provides innovative, accurate
      and safe solutions to surveyors, engineers, developers and civil
      contractors across South Australia.
    </p>
    <p class="support">
      Capabilities included drone capture, GNSS aided processing, survey and
      geospatial analysis. Pixel Surveys projects are always individually
      tailored to meet our clients&rsquo; specific requirements and supported by
      qualified and experienced personnel.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .section {
    padding-block: 56px 80px;
  }

  .grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.4fr 1fr;
    gap: 40px;
    align-items: start;
  }

  /* Large enough to lead the page without being heading-sized: the old 36px
     was set for a short placeholder line, and this sentence at that size would
     dominate everything below it. */
  .lead {
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  /* The placeholder here was underlined, which was fine on a two-word label
     and would read as a broken link on a paragraph. */
  .support {
    font-size: 16.5px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    padding-top: 4px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 24px;
    }
  }
</style>
